  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.add_full_rary_tree - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.add_full_rary_tree.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_full_rary_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Add a full r-ary tree of n nodes to the current graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_full_rary_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Add a full r-ary tree of n nodes to the current graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.add_full_rary_tree()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Add a full r-ary tree of n nodes to the current graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nAdd a full r-ary tree of n nodes to the current graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L10797-L10922){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.add_full_rary_tree(\n    r,\n    n,\n    type=None,\n    label=True,\n    rel=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Full r-ary tree](../assets/graphs/add-full-rary-tree.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three full r-ary trees side by side, roots at the top: a complete binary tree of seven nodes; a binary tree of ten nodes, whose last level is filled from the left and stops partway; and a ternary tree of eight nodes, where the root's first child takes three children and the second child takes the one node left.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nCreates `n` nodes in breadth-first order and makes node `i` a child of node\n`(i - 1) // r`, so every level is filled from left to right before the next one starts.\nEach internal node has `r` children, except possibly the last one, which takes whatever\nnodes are left. This is the shape of a binary heap (`r=2`), and it differs from the\nbalanced tree (see `add_balanced_tree()`) in that you choose the number of nodes rather\nthan the height, so the last level may be only partly filled.\n\nThe root is the first node created. In a directed graph every edge points from parent to\nchild. The tree is appended without touching or connecting to existing nodes, and the\nwhole construction is recorded as a single step.\n\nFull r-ary trees are useful for:\n\n- modeling heaps and other array-backed trees, where a node's children sit at fixed\n  positions\n- hierarchies with a fixed span of control but any total size (an org chart in which\n  every manager has `r` reports)\n- test cases for tree algorithms with an exact node count\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[r]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Branching factor: the number of children of every full internal node. Must be at\n    least `1`; `r=1` produces a path.\n\n<code>[n]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Total number of nodes. Must be at least `1`.\n\n<code>[type]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `type` attribute of every new node. If `None` (default),\n    no `type` attribute is set.\n\n<code>[label]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True` (default), each new node is labelled with its node ID as a string; IDs run\n    in breadth-first order, so the root is `\"1\"` in an empty graph. A label that is\n    already used raises `ValueError` before anything is added. If `False`, the nodes are\n    left unlabelled.\n\n<code>[rel]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `rel` attribute of every new edge. If `None` (default),\n    no `rel` attribute is set.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Self for method chaining. The graph is modified in place.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `r=` or `n=` is less than `1`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~add_balanced_tree`) \n\n:   Add a balanced tree.\n\n[](`~add_binomial_tree`) \n\n:   Add a binomial tree.\n\n[](`~is_tree`) \n\n:   Check whether the graph is a tree.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA full `r`-ary tree of `n` nodes fills each level, every node with `r` children, before it\nstarts the next one. A binary tree of six nodes fills the first two levels and starts the\nthird:\n\n::: {#9a37b78c .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph(directed=True).add_full_rary_tree(r=2, n=6)\n\ngraph.get_edges_str_repr(use_labels=True)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['1->2', '1->3', '2->4', '2->5', '3->6']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nAs in a heap, the children of node `i` are nodes `2i` and `2i + 1`:\n\n::: {#a83b330a .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nsorted(graph.get_label_from_id(n) for n in graph.get_successors(\"2\"))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n['4', '5']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Two children or three\n\nA binary tree on the left and a ternary tree on the right, with `13` nodes and `12` edges\neach. The binary tree needs three levels below the root, and its farthest leaves are `6`\nsteps apart. The ternary tree's two levels are full, and its leaves are at most `4` steps\napart:\n\n::: {#00984d6a .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nbinary = ec.Graph().add_full_rary_tree(r=2, n=13)\nternary = ec.Graph().add_full_rary_tree(r=3, n=13)\n\nbinary.diameter(), ternary.diameter()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(6, 4)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {layout-ncol=\"2\"}\n\n::: {#da588733 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nbinary.layout_kamada_kawai().plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", label_by=\"label\", width=320, height=320, legend=False\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto